  "title": "More models behind one text API",
  "summary": "March made Pollinations easier to use from existing tools, with more model choices, broader audio support, and a growing community directory.\n\nGemini, Qwen reasoning, Mistral Small, and new vision and Roblox-focused options joined the chat lineup. An OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint gave existing clients a familiar way in.\n\nThe text API gained selectable voices and streaming audio. The MCP server grew from image generation to text, speech, and model discovery, then got a clearer package and installation path.\n\nProjects moved higher on the homepage as the directory gained creative apps, bots, tutorials, and SDKs. ComfyUI and OpenWebUI guides offered more ways to connect Pollinations to tools people already use.\n\nModel routing, image fallbacks, and request defaults were adjusted. Cache work for image and text responses, plus a SearchGPT streaming fix, made repeat requests and response formats more predictable.",
